  "metadata": {
    "name": "lax_friedrichs_D_inflow_bc_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/lax_friedrichs_D_inflow_bc: a minimal consuming model binding N=8 at the import edge. The plain match D(u,x) must lower, through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint, to the rule's makearray -- interior [2,7] holding the imported Lax-Friedrichs flux-difference aggregate, the i=1 inflow face holding the flux-difference with the left ghost = gL, the i=8 outflow face holding the flux-difference with the extrapolated ghost u[8] -- with all metaparameters folded, all apply_expression_template nodes (the flux stencil) inlined, and the free names dx and gL surviving in the expanded body. The model declares gL as an ordinary real parameter (the rule's inflow free name). x0 = 0 and dx = 1/8; the dx expression is spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes N before it reaches this document's scope (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings.",
